        "release_date": "1980-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "description": "1. Identify exits: In multi-use facilities, identify the location of emergency exits.\n2. Respond quickly: Know the location of exits in advance so you can respond quickly to an emergency.\n3. Follow directions: In an emergency, follow nearby directions to the exit with the least amount of people.\n4. Go to the opposite exit: If you can't get out of an emergency exit, follow your teacher's directions to the opposite exit.\n5. Open the door: If the door is locked or won't open, you need to ask people around you for help to get out.\n6. Exit the simulation: Press the Next button to exit the simulation.",
